# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; never commit a real key.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A SECRET, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the built JavaScript, so anything here is
# readable by anyone who opens devtools on the deployed site. This file previously held
# VITE_PINATA_JWT, which meant a live upload credential shipped to every visitor.
#
# Uploads now go to an endpoint we control. Its URL is public; the key it holds is not.
# See `server/pin.ts` for the reference implementation, and set PINATA_JWT in the SERVER
# environment - never in a VITE_ variable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the app POSTs images to be pinned. Leave empty and the launch form will say uploads are
# unavailable and take a CID directly, which is the honest degraded state rather than a broken
# button.
#
# Local:  bun server/pin.ts   ->  http://localhost:8787
VITE_PIN_ENDPOINT=
